<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        OPTIONAL / ALTERNATIVE Slovak leave configuration.

        This file ships three kinds of records:

        A) HOLIDAY "full entitlement at start of year" accrual plans  [ARCHIVED]
           An ALTERNATIVE to the default monthly 1/12 dovolenka accrual
           (hr_leave_accrual_plan_data.xml). These grant the WHOLE annual
           entitlement (20 / 25 / 40 days) at once on 1 January
           (frequency='yearly' on 1 Jan, accrued_gain_time='start'). They ship
           ARCHIVED (active=False) so they never interfere with the default
           monthly plans; an administrator archives the monthly plan and
           un-archives the matching year-start plan to switch a company over.

        B) OČR (ošetrovné) statutory-limit plan                       [ACTIVE]
        C) Paid-obstacle (§141) per-reason leave types + annual-limit plans
                                                                      [ACTIVE]
           Ošetrovné is a nemocenská dávka paid by the Sociálna poisťovňa, NOT
           by the employer — the employer only records the absence. hr.leave
           allocations cannot be shipped as install data (employee_id is a
           required field and no employee exists on a fresh install), so the
           statutory day-caps are modelled here as accrual plans whose
           maximum_leave_yearly carries the legal number.

           ONE LEAVE TYPE PER CAPPED REASON (section C). The caps must not
           share a leave type: Odoo pools every allocation of the same type
           into one balance, so hanging 7 + 7 + 10 days off the generic
           OBSTACLE type would enforce a single 24-day pool and let somebody
           book twelve consecutive days of vyšetrenie. Each capped reason
           therefore gets its own leave type with requires_allocation=True,
           which makes the cap a hard limit at booking time.

           The GENERIC l10n_sk_leave_type_obstacle keeps
           requires_allocation=False on purpose: it carries the per-EVENT
           §141 reasons that have no annual quota (svadba, úmrtie, narodenie
           dieťaťa, darovanie krvi §138). Requiring an allocation there would
           make a funeral day unbookable once an unrelated quota ran out.

           All of these carry the same l10n_sk_payroll_code (OBSTACLE), so the
           split is invisible to payroll — the salary rules key on the code,
           not on the leave type.

           OČR (section B) deliberately keeps requires_allocation=False: its
           14-day cap is the krátkodobé ošetrovné, and a hard block would
           reject a legitimate dlhodobé ošetrovné (§42 ods. 5, up to 90 days),
           which is not modelled here.

        =====================================================================
        OČR / ošetrovné — zák. č. 461/2003 Z. z. o sociálnom poistení
        =====================================================================
          * Krátkodobé ošetrovné (§39 ods. 1 písm. a, §42 ods. 4): dávka zo
            Sociálnej poisťovne, najviac 14 KALENDÁRNYCH DNÍ od vzniku potreby
            osobného a celodenného ošetrovania/starostlivosti. (2025/2026)
          * Dlhodobé ošetrovné (§39 ods. 1 písm. b, §42 ods. 5): v úhrne najviac
            90 DNÍ za 12 mesiacov od vzniku prvého nároku; vystriedanie
            poistencov v tom istom prípade najskôr po 30 dňoch.
          * Oprávnené osoby (§39): dieťa, manžel/manželka, rodič, rodič
            manžela/manželky a ďalší vymedzení rodinní príslušníci.
          => Cap encoded below = 14 (krátkodobé). The 90-day dlhodobé limit is
             a Sociálna poisťovňa benefit duration, documented here only.

        =====================================================================
        Prekážky v práci s náhradou mzdy — §141 (a §138) Zákonníka práce,
        zák. č. 311/2001 Z. z.  (dôležité osobné prekážky v práci)
        =====================================================================
        Reason                                | Limit / rok | Náhrada mzdy
        ......................................|.............|..............
        Vyšetrenie/ošetrenie v zdrav. zar.    | 7 dní       | ÁNO (platené)
        Sprevádzanie rodinného príslušníka    | 7 dní       | ÁNO (platené)
        Sprevádzanie zdrav. postih. dieťaťa   | 10 dní      | ÁNO (platené)
        Vlastná svadba                        | 1 deň       | ÁNO (platené)
        Svadba dieťaťa/rodiča                 | 1 deň       | NIE
        Úmrtie manžela/dieťaťa                | 2 dni +1deň | ÁNO (platené)
                                              | na pohreb   |
        Úmrtie rodiča/súrodenca               | 1 deň (+1   | ÁNO (platené)
                                              | ak zariaďuje|
                                              | pohreb)     |
        Úmrtie prarodiča/vnuka/inej bl. osoby | najviac 1 d | ÁNO (platené)
        Narodenie dieťaťa (preprava manželky) | nevyhn. čas | ÁNO (platené)
        Sťahovanie v tej istej obci           | 1 deň       | NIE (bez náhr.)
        Sťahovanie do inej obce               | 2 dni       | NIE (bez náhr.)
        Darovanie krvi / biol. materiálu(§138)| nevyhn. čas | ÁNO (platené)

        The three reasons carrying a concrete ANNUAL number (vyšetrenie 7 dní,
        sprevádzanie 7 dní, sprevádzanie ZŤP dieťaťa 10 dní) each get their own
        leave type + plan below. The remaining one/two-day reasons are
        PER-EVENT, not annual caps, so they are booked against the generic
        l10n_sk_leave_type_obstacle, which needs no allocation.

        Sources (confirmed 2025/2026):
          - Zákon č. 461/2003 Z. z. §39, §42 (Slov-Lex; Sociálna poisťovňa)
          - Zákonník práce §138, §141 (Slov-Lex 311/2001 Z. z.)
          - podnikajte.sk — Prekážky v práci (§141, §142)
          - socpoist.sk — Ošetrovné (krátkodobé/dlhodobé)
        Note: novela ZP účinná od 1.1.2026 rozšírila §141 ods. 2 písm. c);
        day-limits above are unchanged. Human review recommended before use.
    -->

    <!-- ============================================================== -->
    <!-- A) HOLIDAY: full annual entitlement granted on 1 January       -->
    <!--    ARCHIVED alternative to the monthly 1/12 accrual plans.     -->
    <!-- ============================================================== -->

    <!-- 20 dní (4 týždne, §103 ods. 1) granted on 1 Jan -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_4w" model="hr.leave.accrual.plan">
        <field name="name">Annual leave — 20 days, full grant on 1 January (archived)</field>
        <field name="time_off_type_id" ref="l10n_sk_leave_type_dovolenka"/>
        <field name="accrued_gain_time">start</field>
        <field name="carryover_date">year_start</field>
        <field name="can_be_carryover" eval="True"/>
        <field name="active" eval="False"/>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_level_dovolenka_start_4w" model="hr.leave.accrual.level">
        <field name="accrual_plan_id" ref="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_4w"/>
        <field name="added_value">20</field>
        <field name="added_value_type">day</field>
        <field name="frequency">yearly</field>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time" eval="False"/>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time_yearly" eval="True"/>
        <field name="maximum_leave_yearly">20</field>
        <field name="action_with_unused_accruals">all</field>
        <!-- §113: unused dovolenka carried into the following year is forfeited
             if still unused a year later. accrual_validity counts 364 days from the
             1 Jan carryover, so the window closes ~31 Dec, just before the next
             1 Jan carryover -> a clean one-year forfeit every cycle. -->
        <field name="accrual_validity" eval="True"/>
        <field name="accrual_validity_count">364</field>
        <field name="accrual_validity_type">day</field>
    </record>

    <!-- 25 dní (5 týždňov, §103 ods. 2) granted on 1 Jan -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_5w" model="hr.leave.accrual.plan">
        <field name="name">Annual leave — 25 days, full grant on 1 January (archived)</field>
        <field name="time_off_type_id" ref="l10n_sk_leave_type_dovolenka"/>
        <field name="accrued_gain_time">start</field>
        <field name="carryover_date">year_start</field>
        <field name="can_be_carryover" eval="True"/>
        <field name="active" eval="False"/>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_level_dovolenka_start_5w" model="hr.leave.accrual.level">
        <field name="accrual_plan_id" ref="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_5w"/>
        <field name="added_value">25</field>
        <field name="added_value_type">day</field>
        <field name="frequency">yearly</field>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time" eval="False"/>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time_yearly" eval="True"/>
        <field name="maximum_leave_yearly">25</field>
        <field name="action_with_unused_accruals">all</field>
        <!-- §113: one-year carryover window, then forfeit (364 days from carryover, so it expires ~31 Dec, just before the next 1 Jan carryover). -->
        <field name="accrual_validity" eval="True"/>
        <field name="accrual_validity_count">364</field>
        <field name="accrual_validity_type">day</field>
    </record>

    <!-- 40 dní (8 týždňov, §103 ods. 3) granted on 1 Jan -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_8w" model="hr.leave.accrual.plan">
        <field name="name">Annual leave — 40 days, full grant on 1 January (archived)</field>
        <field name="time_off_type_id" ref="l10n_sk_leave_type_dovolenka"/>
        <field name="accrued_gain_time">start</field>
        <field name="carryover_date">year_start</field>
        <field name="can_be_carryover" eval="True"/>
        <field name="active" eval="False"/>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_level_dovolenka_start_8w" model="hr.leave.accrual.level">
        <field name="accrual_plan_id" ref="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_dovolenka_start_8w"/>
        <field name="added_value">40</field>
        <field name="added_value_type">day</field>
        <field name="frequency">yearly</field>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time" eval="False"/>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time_yearly" eval="True"/>
        <field name="maximum_leave_yearly">40</field>
        <field name="action_with_unused_accruals">all</field>
        <!-- §113: one-year carryover window, then forfeit (364 days from carryover, so it expires ~31 Dec, just before the next 1 Jan carryover). -->
        <field name="accrual_validity" eval="True"/>
        <field name="accrual_validity_count">364</field>
        <field name="accrual_validity_type">day</field>
    </record>

    <!-- ============================================================== -->
    <!-- B) OČR: krátkodobé ošetrovné cap = 14 dní (SP benefit)  ACTIVE -->
    <!-- ============================================================== -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_ocr_short_14d" model="hr.leave.accrual.plan">
        <field name="name">Short-term family care (OČR) — 14 days/year limit</field>
        <field name="time_off_type_id" ref="l10n_sk_leave_type_ocr"/>
        <field name="accrued_gain_time">start</field>
        <field name="carryover_date">year_start</field>
        <field name="can_be_carryover" eval="False"/>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_level_ocr_short_14d" model="hr.leave.accrual.level">
        <field name="accrual_plan_id" ref="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_ocr_short_14d"/>
        <field name="added_value">14</field>
        <field name="added_value_type">day</field>
        <field name="frequency">yearly</field>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time" eval="False"/>
        <field name="cap_accrued_time_yearly" eval="True"/>
        <field name="maximum_leave_yearly">14</field>
        <field name="action_with_unused_accruals">lost</field>
    </record>

    <!-- ============================================================== -->
    <!-- C) Paid obstacles §141 - annual caps                    ACTIVE -->
    <!-- ============================================================== -->

    <!-- One leave type per capped reason, each with requires_allocation=True
         so the statutory day-cap is enforced when the leave is booked. They
         all carry the OBSTACLE payroll code, so the payslip cannot tell them
         apart from the generic paid obstacle. -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_leave_type_obstacle_exam" model="hr.leave.type">
        <field name="name">Paid Obstacle — Medical Examination (7 days/year)</field>
        <field name="l10n_sk_payroll_code">OBSTACLE</field>
        <field name="country_id" ref="base.sk"/>
        <field name="company_id" eval="False"/>
        <field name="requires_allocation" eval="True"/>
        <field name="request_unit">day</field>
        <field name="leave_validation_type">no_validation</field>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_leave_type_obstacle_accompany" model="hr.leave.type">
        <field name="name">Paid Obstacle — Accompanying a Family Member (7 days/year)</field>
        <field name="l10n_sk_payroll_code">OBSTACLE</field>
        <field name="country_id" ref="base.sk"/>
        <field name="company_id" eval="False"/>
        <field name="requires_allocation" eval="True"/>
        <field name="request_unit">day</field>
        <field name="leave_validation_type">no_validation</field>
    </record>
    <record id="l10n_sk_leave_type_obstacle_accompany_disabled" model="hr.leave.type">
        <field name="name">Paid Obstacle — Accompanying a Disabled Child ZŤP (10 days/year)</field>
        <field name="l10n_sk_payroll_code">OBSTACLE</field>
        <field name="country_id" ref="base.sk"/>
        <field name="company_id" eval="False"/>
        <field name="requires_allocation" eval="True"/>
        <field name="request_unit">day</field>
        <field name="leave_validation_type">no_validation</field>
    </record>

    <!-- Vyšetrenie/ošetrenie v zdravotníckom zariadení: 7 dní/rok -->
    <record id="l10n_sk_accrual_plan_obstacle_exam_7d" model="hr.leave.accrual.plan">
